{
  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "Herdr Mobile Relay REST API",
    "version": "1.0.7",
    "description": "# Build against Herdr Mobile Relay\n\nThis reference describes the HTTP control-plane API. The relay always binds to loopback; when it is reached over Tailscale Serve, configure a trusted Tailscale user and use the same HTTPS origin for the documentation and API.\n\n## Authentication and authorization\n\nDirect calls to `127.0.0.1` are local-operator calls. Remote requests must pass the configured Tailscale identity gate (`Tailscale-User-Login` by default). Write operations additionally require a device authorized by the optional device policy. Browser writes must be same-origin; native clients without an `Origin` send `X-Herdr-Client: herdr-mobile-v1`.\n\nAll session-scoped REST routes accept optional `?session=<name>`. Omit it to use the primary Herdr session. IDs returned by snapshots are opaque and must be URL encoded when inserted into a path.\n\n## WebSocket interfaces\n\n- **`/api/live`** \u2014 raw terminal/control WebSocket. Upgrade a GET request after passing the same access checks. Server messages: `connected`, `source_status`, `snapshot_changed`, `pane_output_changed`, `pane_stream_status`, and `pane_frame`. Client commands: `watch_pane` and `scroll_pane`. This is the low-level terminal fallback.\n- **`/acp`** \u2014 ACP v2-style JSON-RPC 2.0 WebSocket. Text frames only; 256 KiB maximum inbound frame; batches rejected. The first request is `initialize`; then use `session/list`, `session/resume`, `session/new`, `session/prompt`, `session/close`, and `session/cancel`. Read the full [ACP WebSocket guide](https://github.com/bejorock/herdr-plugin-mobile-relay/blob/main/docs/ACP_API.md) before implementing a client.\n\nOpenAPI does not model either WebSocket protocol.\n\n## Errors\n\nRoute and validation errors use a non-2xx status. JSON errors normally use `{ \"error\": \"\u2026\" }`; a few legacy endpoint errors are plain text. Mutations return an `ActionResponse` body for a Herdr-side failure. If `deliveryAmbiguous` or `textDelivered` is true, inspect the terminal state before retrying."
  },
  "servers": [
    {
      "url": "/",
      "description": "Same origin as the relay UI"
    }
  ],
